# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Second Brain Generator — .gitignore
# Secrets and OS files must NEVER be committed.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Secrets & credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*_token
*_secret
credentials.json
secrets.json
.netrc

# ── macOS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# ── Editors ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ── Obsidian ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
vault/.obsidian/

# ── Claude Code — non-portable local files ──────────────────────────
.claude/settings.local.json
# Local instructions auto-loaded by Claude Code (personal override, not committed).
# In THIS repo we use it for the DEV context (an @DEVELOPING.md), which therefore
# must NOT ship with "Use this template".
CLAUDE.local.md

# ── Files generated by installer.mjs (contain an absolute path, ─────────
#    machine-specific → regenerated on each clone, never committed)
.mcp.json
.claude/settings.json
# The engine's copy of settings.json (same reason as the line above: absolute paths belonging to THIS machine — never commit it).
.engine-base/.claude/settings.json
# NB: CLAUDE.md is generated by the installer but does NOT contain an absolute path.
# Deliberately left committable: it's your constitution, it must travel between
# your machines. (In THIS template repo there's only CLAUDE.md.template.)

# ── Node / RAG ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
rag/.cache/
rag/dist/
local-mirror/dist/
# Local-mirror single-flight lockfiles — per-process, per-machine, ephemeral (never commit).
# The sidecar state.json alongside them IS committed on purpose; only the locks are transient.
.local-mirror/*.sync.lock
# Transient per-brain health-check verdict (ADR 0028) — regenerated each session.
engine-health.json
# Universes (ADR 0034): NOTHING under .vault-rag/ is ignored, on purpose. Both the
# registry (which universes exist) and the active-universe pointer (which one you
# are in) are the OWNER's state, not the machine's — your connectors already follow
# you from laptop to laptop, so your retrieval scope must too. Do not "restore" an
# ignore line here for consistency with the caches below; a test enforces it
# (scripts/lib/universes.test.mjs).

# ── Mutation testing (dev-only, maintainers/mutation) ───────────────
# Stryker working dir + generated reports. The scores live in the plan, not git.
maintainers/mutation/.stryker-tmp/
# The generated HTML dashboards stay out: ~1 MB each, unreadable in a diff, and
# fully regenerable from the run. The .log files DO ship (see the negation in the
# Misc block below): RESULTS.md cites them as evidence, and their survivor lists
# are the raw material of RETROSPECTIVE.md. Re-deriving one costs a 13-min re-run.
maintainers/mutation/reports/*.html

# ── Misc ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
# …except the mutation run logs, which are evidence rather than debris. This
# negation must stay AFTER `*.log`: the last matching pattern wins.
!maintainers/mutation/reports/*.log
.cache/
tmp/

# QA feedback dumps that may contain confidential source data — never commit
maintainers/qa/_private/

# Generated engine health-check report (like engine-health.json above)
vault/engine-health/
